   "he": "הַכַּלָּה הוֹפֶכֶת אֶת פָּנֶיהָ וְכוּ׳. מַאי טַעְמָא? אָמַר רַבִּי חִיָּיא בַּר אַבָּא אָמַר רַבִּי יוֹחָנָן: מִפְּנֵי שֶׁהִיא בּוֹשָׁה.",
   "en": "It was taught in the mishna that «a bride turns her face.» The Gemara asks: «What is the reason» she turns her face? «Rabbi Ḥiyya bar Abba said» that «Rabbi Yoḥanan said: It is because she is embarrassed» by other members of the group looking at her."
